#[chapter/15/lore]{
  notes: [
    "Bonk City has no straight streets; every road bends twice so that you arrive facing the plaza. A straight line comes out at the back wall, at the low parcel gate."
    "A bronze post that leaned for two hundred years stands upright after the figure passes it."
    "The parcel gate fits the figure and not his hat. The porter holds the gate against a thirty-year rule; the feast flour is spoiled; he signs the damage in his own name. The hat goes over t..."
    "Under the gate the figure retrieves a horn button lost in the plaza long ago: round, with two holes."
    "Three honest records: the gate-book says parcel, the carpenter's log says door (opens inward), the night school's roll says child (name left blank)."
    "Mx. BoneWAP pins all three side by side and will not take any of them down."
    "By one o'clock the city decides the destined one is the dog, and seats Boof at the second place."
    "The figure stands a quarter turn away from the feast, watching the woman who washes the plates."
  ]
}

